{"title":"Career Roadmap · System Administrator","role":"System Administrator","summary":"A System Administrator (SysAdmin) manages and maintains an organization's computing infrastructure, including servers, operating systems, networks, users, storage, backups, security, monitoring, and IT services.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Computer Science"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A System Administrator (SysAdmin) manages and maintains an organization's computing infrastructure, including servers, operating systems, networks, users, storage, backups, security, monitoring, and IT services."},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc. Computer Science graduate has a strong foundation for this role through:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Operating systems"},{"text":"Computer networks"},{"text":"Databases"},{"text":"Programming"},{"text":"Computer architecture"},{"text":"Cybersecurity fundamentals"},{"text":"Troubleshooting"},{"text":"Cloud computing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A modern System Administrator is no longer limited to manually configuring physical servers. The role increasingly includes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Linux administration"},{"text":"Windows Server"},{"text":"Cloud infrastructure"},{"text":"Virtualization"},{"text":"Identity and access management"},{"text":"Automation"},{"text":"Monitoring"},{"text":"Backup and disaster recovery"},{"text":"Infrastructure as Code"},{"text":"Containers"},{"text":"Security"},{"text":"DevOps/SRE practices"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest long-term positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Linux","Networking","Cloud","Security","Automation","Monitoring","Infrastructure as Code"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{